[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have enough information to provide a comprehensive summary. Let me compile the findings:\n\n## Plan Import Implementation Architecture - Comprehensive Summary\n\nBased on my thorough exploration of the kspec project, here's the complete architecture of the plan import system:\n\n### 1. Plan Import Command Handler\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/cli/commands/plan-import.ts`\n\nThe entry point is `registerPlanImportCommand()` which registers the `kspec plan import <path>` command with these options:\n- `--module <ref>` (required) - Module to add specs under (e.g., `@core-module`)\n- `--dry-run` - Show what would be created without making changes\n- `--update` - Update existing specs instead of skipping them\n- `--json` - Output as JSON\n\nThe main workflow in `importPlan()` follows 8 key phases:\n\n**Phase 1: Parse & Validate**\n- Reads plan file from disk\n- Calls `parsePlanDocument(content)` to extract specs, tasks, and implementation notes\n- Reports YAML parse errors (fatal) and validation errors (non-fatal, collected)\n\n**Phase 2: Load Project State**\n- Loads existing plans via `loadPlans(ctx)`\n- Builds reference indexes via `buildIndexes(ctx, plans)` to check for slug collisions\n- Validates the target module exists and is type \"module\"\n\n**Phase 3: Parent Validation & Topological Sort**\n- Validates all parent references exist (checks in project or in same import via `validateParentRefs()`)\n- Detects circular dependencies via `topologicalSort()` (fatal error)\n- Sorts specs in topological order (parents before children) so specs can be created in correct order\n\n**Phase 4: Create Plan Record**\n- Generates plan slug with \"plan-\" prefix to prevent collision with specs\n- Creates plan with `createPlan()` input containing title, content, status, source_path, and slugs\n- Attaches global implementation notes to plan record as a note entry\n- Reserves all generated slugs to prevent collisions during spec/task creation\n\n**Phase 5: Create Specs**\n- Iterates through topologically sorted specs\n- For each spec:\n  - Validates required `title` field\n  - Generates slug from title if not provided (kebab-case, max 50 chars)\n  - Checks for slug collisions (within import + existing refs)\n  - Resolves parent reference (checks created specs map first, then existing project specs)\n  - Creates spec item with `createSpecItem()` input\n  - Adds spec to parent (or module) using `addChildItem()`\n  - Tracks created specs in map for parent resolution in later specs\n  - Handles root-level traits (type: trait, no parent) → added to kynetic.yaml project-level traits array\n- Logs errors for specs with missing fields or parent references (non-fatal, collected)\n\n**Phase 6: Derive Tasks from Specs**\n- Only if `parsed.tasks.derive_from_specs === true` AND specs were created\n- For each created spec:\n  - Generates task title as \"Implement {spec.title}\"\n  - Generates task slug from title (kebab-case)\n  - Ensures slug uniqueness across all namespaces\n  - Creates task with `createTask()` input containing:\n    - spec_ref: reference to the spec\n    - plan_ref: reference to the plan\n    - priority: 3 (default)\n  - Attaches scoped implementation notes:\n    - If spec has `implementation_notes`, attaches those to this task\n    - Otherwise, attaches plan-level implementation notes with plan reference\n- Saves task via `saveTask()` and updates plan's `derived_tasks` array\n\n**Phase 7: Create Additional Manual Tasks**\n- If `parsed.tasks.additional_tasks` array exists\n- For each manual task definition:\n  - Creates task with `createTask()` input\n  - Uses provided priority or defaults to 3\n  - Optionally links to a spec via `spec_ref` if provided\n  - Stores task description in notes\n  - Saves task and updates plan's `derived_tasks` array\n\n**Phase 8: Persist & Output**\n- Saves plan record via `savePlan()` to `.kspec/project.plans.yaml`\n- Auto-commits to shadow branch via `commitIfShadow()` with message type \"plan-import\"\n- Outputs summary (human-readable or JSON) with created/updated items, errors, and skipped items\n- Exits with code 0 (success) whether or not errors occurred\n\n---\n\n### 2. Plan Document Parsing\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/parser/plan-document.ts`\n\nThe parser extracts structured data from markdown files with these sections:\n\n**Document Structure**:\n```\n# Title\n## Specs\n```yaml\n- title: ...\n  slug: ...\n  type: ...\n  parent: ...\n  description: ...\n  acceptance_criteria: [...]\n  traits: [...]\n  implementation_notes: |\n    Multi-line notes\n```\n## Tasks\nderive_from_specs: true\n```yaml\n- title: ...\n  slug: ...\n  priority: ...\n  tags: [...]\n  spec_ref: ...\n  description: ...\n```\n## Implementation Notes\nGlobal notes for all tasks without per-spec notes.\n```\n\n**Parser Functions**:\n\n1. **`parsePlanDocument(content: string)`** - Main entry point\n   - Extracts title from first `# Heading`\n   - Calls `extractSpecsSection()` to get specs array\n   - Calls `extractTasksSection()` to get task config\n   - Calls `extractImplementationNotes()` to get global notes\n   - Returns `ParsedPlanDocument` with specs, tasks, implementationNotes, and error array\n\n2. **`extractSpecsSection()`** - Finds `## Specs` section, extracts YAML block\n   - Looks for `## Specs\\n```yaml\\n...\\n```\\n`\n   - Parses YAML array with `parseYaml()`\n   - Validates each spec with `PlanSpecSchema` (Zod)\n   - Returns array of validated specs (skips invalid ones, logs errors)\n\n3. **`extractTasksSection()`** - Finds `## Tasks` section\n   - Looks for `derive_from_specs: true|false` flag\n   - Looks for `## Tasks\\n```yaml\\n...\\n```\\n` for additional_tasks array\n   - Validates each task with `PlanTaskSchema` (Zod)\n   - Returns `TasksSection` with both fields\n\n4. **`extractImplementationNotes()`** - Finds `## Implementation Notes` section\n   - Returns text content between `##` markers (plain text, not YAML)\n   - Returns null if not found\n\n5. **`topologicalSort(specs: PlanSpec[])`** - Orders specs by parent dependencies\n   - Detects duplicate slugs (error)\n   - Builds parent-child adjacency graph from `spec.parent` fields (local refs only)\n   - Detects cycles via DFS (error: \"Circular parent reference\")\n   - Returns sorted array with parents before children\n   - Uses DFS post-order traversal for consistent ordering\n\n6. **`validateParentRefs(specs, existingRefs)`** - Validates parent references exist\n   - Checks each parent against plan-local specs and existing project refs\n   - Returns array of dependency errors (non-fatal)\n\n**PlanSpec Schema** (from plan documents):\n```typescript\n{\n  title: string (required)\n  slug?: string\n  type?: string (feature, requirement, trait, etc.)\n  parent?: string (reference to another spec, with or without @)\n  description?: string\n  acceptance_criteria?: AcceptanceCriterion[]\n  traits?: string[] (array of trait references)\n  implementation_notes?: string\n}\n```\n\n**PlanTask Schema** (for additional_tasks):\n```typescript\n{\n  title: string (required)\n  slug?: string\n  priority?: number (1-5)\n  tags?: string[]\n  description?: string (stored in task notes)\n  spec_ref?: string (optional link to a spec)\n}\n```\n\n**TasksSection Schema**:\n```typescript\n{\n  derive_from_specs?: boolean\n  additional_tasks?: PlanTask[]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Spec Item Schema & Creation\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/schema/spec.ts`\n\nThe full `SpecItemSchema` defines spec items with fields:\n\n**Identity**:\n- `_ulid` - Unique identifier (auto-generated)\n- `slugs` - Array of human-friendly references\n- `title` - Required display name\n\n**Classification**:\n- `type` - ItemTypeSchema (feature, requirement, constraint, decision, module, trait, risk, milestone)\n- `priority` - PrioritySchema (1-5)\n- `tags` - String array for categorization\n- `status` - Optional StatusSchema with:\n  - `maturity` (draft, proposed, approved, implemented, deprecated)\n  - `implementation` (not_started, in_progress, complete, blocked)\n\n**Content**:\n- `description` - Brief explanation\n- `acceptance_criteria` - Array of acceptance criteria with Given/When/Then format:\n  ```typescript\n  {\n    id: string\n    given: string\n    when: string\n    then: string\n  }\n  ```\n\n**Relationships**:\n- `depends_on` - Array of references to prerequisite specs\n- `implements` - Array of references to requirements it implements\n- `relates_to` - Array of related spec references\n- `tests` - Array of test references\n- `traits` - Array of trait references it adheres to\n- `supersedes` - Single reference to spec it replaces\n\n**Traceability** (optional):\n- `traceability` - Object with:\n  - `implementation` - Array of code locations\n  - `tests` - Array of test file paths\n  - `commits` - Array of commit hashes\n  - `issues` - Array of issue references\n\n**Lifecycle**:\n- `created`, `created_by` - When and who created\n- `deprecated_in`, `superseded_by` - Deprecation tracking\n- `verified_at`, `verified_by` - Verification metadata\n\n**Notes** - Array of NoteSchema entries (append-only work log)\n\n**Creation via `createSpecItem(input: SpecItemInput)`**:\n- Generates ULID if not provided\n- Defaults empty arrays to []\n- Defaults created timestamp to now\n- All other fields passed through or remain undefined\n\n---\n\n### 4. Task Schema & Creation\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/schema/task.ts`\n\nThe full `TaskSchema` defines task items with fields:\n\n**Identity**:\n- `_ulid` - Unique identifier (auto-generated)\n- `slugs` - Array of human-friendly references\n- `title` - Required display name\n- `type` - TaskTypeSchema (task, bug, spike, meta)\n\n**Relationships** (Key for plan import):\n- `spec_ref` - Reference to spec this task implements (nullable, optional)\n- `plan_ref` - Reference to plan this task was derived from (nullable, optional)\n- `meta_ref` - Reference to workflow/convention for process tracking (nullable, optional)\n- `origin` - How task was created (manual, derived, observation_promotion)\n\n**Dependencies** (Critical for task ordering):\n- `depends_on` - Array of RefSchema (references to prerequisite tasks)\n- `blocked_by` - Array of strings (human-readable blocking reasons)\n- `context` - Array of related references for context\n\n**Status**:\n- `status` - TaskStatusSchema (pending, in_progress, pending_review, completed, blocked, cancelled)\n- `closed_reason` - Reason for completion/cancellation\n\n**Work Metadata**:\n- `priority` - 1-5 (default 3)\n- `complexity` - Optional 1-5 scale\n- `tags` - String array\n- `assignee` - Optional person\n\n**Automation** (optional):\n- `automation` - AutomationStatusSchema (eligible, needs_review, manual_only) or unset (unassessed)\n\n**Tracking**:\n- `vcs_refs` - Array of VCS branch/commit references\n- `created_at`, `started_at`, `submitted_at`, `completed_at` - Timestamps\n- `notes` - Array of NoteSchema (append-only work log)\n- `todos` - Array of lightweight checklist items\n\n**Creation via `createTask(input: TaskInput)`**:\n- Generates ULID if not provided\n- Sets status to \"pending\" if not provided\n- Sets priority to 3 if not provided\n- Defaults empty arrays and relationships to []\n- Sets created_at to now if not provided\n\n**Plan Import Task Creation Pattern**:\n```typescript\nconst taskInput: TaskInput = {\n  title: `Implement ${spec.title}`,  // Pattern: \"Implement X\"\n  type: \"task\",\n  spec_ref: `@${specSlug}`,           // Links to spec\n  plan_ref: planRef,                  // Links to plan\n  priority: 3,                         // Default priority\n  slugs: [uniqueSlug],                // Auto-generated slug\n  tags: [],                            // From manual task def if provided\n  depends_on: [],                      // Not auto-filled from spec dependencies\n  notes: [],                           // Contains implementation notes\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Task Derivation & Spec-to-Task Flow\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/cli/commands/derive.ts`\n\nWhile plan import has built-in derivation logic, the separate `derive` command provides general spec-to-task derivation:\n\n**Key Concepts**:\n- **Parent-Child Hierarchy**: Specs maintain hierarchy via `_path` metadata (e.g., `features[0].requirements[1]`)\n- **Topological Order**: When deriving from a spec, parent tasks are created before child tasks\n- **Direct Children Only**: `isDirectChildOf()` checks path structure to find only immediate children\n\n**Spec Hierarchy Navigation**:\n- `getParentPath(childPath)` - Extracts parent path from child's _path\n- `findParentItem(item, allItems)` - Finds parent spec by path matching\n- `getDirectChildren(parent, allItems)` - Gets only immediate children\n- `collectItemsRecursively(root, allItems)` - Gets root + all descendants in order\n\n**Task Slug Generation**:\n```typescript\n// From spec title \"My Feature\" → \"task-my-feature\"\nfunction generateSlugFromTitle(title: string): string {\n  return \"task-\" + title\n    .toLowerCase()\n    .replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, \"-\")\n    .replace(/^-|-$/g, \"\")\n    .slice(0, 50);\n}\n```\n\n**Priority Conversion**: Spec priority converted to task priority (both 1-5 scale)\n\n---\n\n### 6. Reference Index & Slug Management\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/parser/refs.ts`\n\nThe `ReferenceIndex` class handles spec/task/plan lookups by ULID or slug:\n\n**Created via `buildIndexes(ctx, plans)`**:\n```typescript\nconst { refIndex, itemIndex, traitIndex, tasks, items } = \n  await buildIndexes(ctx, plans);\n```\n\nReturns:\n- `refIndex: ReferenceIndex` - Resolves refs across all namespaces\n- `itemIndex: Index<LoadedSpecItem>` - Spec-specific index\n- `traitIndex: TraitIndex` - Trait hierarchy\n- `tasks: LoadedTask[]` - All tasks\n- `items: LoadedSpecItem[]` - All specs\n\n**Key Methods**:\n- `resolve(ref: string)` - Resolves @slug or ULID, returns `{ ok: boolean, item?, ulid?, error?, candidates? }`\n- `isSlugAvailable(slug)` - Checks if slug is unused across all namespaces (plans, specs, tasks)\n- `shortUlid(ulid)` - Returns first 8 chars of ULID for display\n\n**Namespace Hierarchy**:\n1. Specs (all items from .kspec/modules/*.yaml)\n2. Tasks (all items from .kspec/project.tasks.yaml)\n3. Plans (all items from .kspec/project.plans.yaml)\n\nPlan import includes plans in index during creation to detect cross-namespace slug collisions.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Spec/Task Persistence\n\n**Files**: \n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/parser/yaml.ts` - YAML I/O\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/parser/plans.ts` - Plan persistence\n\n**Spec Creation & Storage**:\n- `createSpecItem()` - Creates in-memory spec\n- `addChildItem(ctx, parent, child)` - Adds child to parent's array field\n  - Loads parent's source file\n  - Appends to appropriate field (features, requirements, traits, etc.)\n  - Writes back preserving format\n  - Returns item with _sourceFile and _path metadata\n\n**Task Creation & Storage**:\n- `createTask()` - Creates in-memory task\n- `saveTask(ctx, task)` - Saves to file\n  - Uses task._sourceFile if present, otherwise defaults to project.tasks.yaml\n  - Supports both array format and { tasks: [...] } wrapper format\n  - Atomic read-modify-write to prevent TOCTOU\n  - Preserves formatting\n\n**Plan Creation & Storage**:\n- `createPlan()` - Creates in-memory plan with defaults\n- `savePlan(ctx, plan)` - Saves to .kspec/project.plans.yaml\n  - File-lock based concurrency (mkdir atomicity)\n  - PID-based staleness detection\n  - Atomic read-modify-write\n  - Format preservation\n\n---\n\n### 8. Plan Import Tests\n\n**Files**:\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/tests/cli-plan-import.test.ts` - Integration tests\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/tests/plan-document-parser.test.ts` - Parser unit tests\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/tests/task-plan-ref.test.ts` - Task plan_ref field tests\n\n**Test Coverage** (via AC annotations):\n- ac-11: Parse ## Specs YAML blocks ✓\n- ac-12: Auto-derive tasks when derive_from_specs=true ✓\n- ac-13: Extract global & per-spec implementation notes ✓\n- ac-14: Skip existing specs by default ✓\n- ac-15: Dry-run mode (no changes, exit 0) ✓\n- ac-16: Topological sort (parents before children) ✓\n- ac-17: Detect missing parent references ✓\n- ac-18: Detect circular parent dependencies ✓\n- ac-19: Tasks link to specs and plans ✓\n- ac-20: Task title pattern \"Implement X\" ✓\n- ac-21: Report YAML parse errors (fatal) ✓\n- ac-22: Validate required fields ✓\n- ac-23: Summary output with counts & errors ✓\n- ac-24: Auto-commit to shadow branch ✓\n- ac-25: Skip existing specs ✓\n- ac-26: --update flag updates existing specs ✓\n- ac-27: Additional manual tasks ✓\n- ac-28: Plan slug auto-generation with \"plan-\" prefix ✓\n- ac-29: Collect errors and continue ✓\n- ac-30: JSON output mode ✓\n- ac-31: Tasks display plan_ref ✓\n- ac-32: JSON output includes created/updated/errors ✓\n- ac-33: Error hints for missing parents ✓\n\n---\n\n### 9. Key Architectural Decisions\n\n**Plan Slug Namespacing**:\n- Plans auto-generate slugs with \"plan-\" prefix (e.g., \"plan-test-plan\")\n- Prevents collision with spec slugs (which have no prefix by default)\n- Checked against all namespaces (specs + tasks + plans)\n\n**Scope of Implementation Notes**:\n- **Global notes** (## Implementation Notes) → Added to plan record as a note\n- **Per-spec notes** (spec.implementation_notes) → Added to that spec's derived task\n- **Fallback** (no per-spec notes) → Task gets note referencing plan with global notes\n\n**Task Derivation Pattern**:\n- One task per created spec\n- Task title: \"Implement {spec.title}\"\n- Task always links both spec_ref AND plan_ref\n- Task notes contain implementation guidance\n\n**Error Handling**:\n- YAML parse errors: Fatal (exit 1)\n- Validation errors: Non-fatal (collected, printed, but continues)\n- Missing parent errors: Non-fatal (spec skipped with reason)\n- Slug collision errors: Non-fatal (spec skipped with reason)\n\n**Ordering Guarantee**:\n- Specs created in topological order (parents first)\n- Ensures parent resolution during creation\n- Tasks derived in order specs were created\n- Manual tasks created last\n\n**Reference Resolution**:\n- `spec.parent` resolved first against specs being created (createdSpecsMap)\n- Then against existing project specs (refIndex)\n- Supports both @slug and bare slug formats (normalizeRefInput strips @ prefix)\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\nThe plan import system is a complete translation layer that:\n\n1. **Parses** structured markdown plan documents (specs, tasks, notes sections)\n2. **Validates** YAML syntax, required fields, and references\n3. **Detects** circular dependencies and missing parents\n4. **Orders** specs topologically so parents exist before children\n5. **Creates** spec items in the project hierarchy\n6. **Derives** tasks automatically (one per spec) or manually (user-defined)\n7. **Attaches** implementation guidance as notes (global or per-spec)\n8. **Links** tasks to both specs and the plan record\n9. **Prevents** slug collisions across all namespaces (specs/tasks/plans)\n10. **Persists** atomically with format preservation\n11. **Auto-commits** to shadow branch for audit trail\n12. **Reports** comprehensive results (created/updated/errors/skipped)\n\nThe architecture prioritizes **data integrity** (topological ordering, collision detection, atomic writes), **auditability** (auto-commits, error collection), and **flexibility** (dry-run, update mode, manual task definitions, per-spec vs global notes)."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ad4fe3a (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 65402\ntool_uses: 25\nduration_ms: 70921</usage>"}]